<%# One section of the character sheet: its title, then its fields laid out by their types (sheet_section_layout).
    No line between the sections (decision): the titles and the space are enough. lead: optional, what opens the
    section before its fields (the name of the character, in the first section); a section in columns puts it at the
    top of the column of its fields, and so does the column of the lists when the picks stand beside them
    (sheet_lead_in_lists_column?).
    The legend floats, so that it sits in the section and not in the border of the fieldset (see the choice rows).
    page_title: optional, the title of the page; a section of the same name keeps its title for screen readers only
    ("Personnage" twice, decision). side_by_side: the sections of the step stand in columns, no space above.
    The saving throws and the skills are titled in small capitals, as on a character sheet %>
<% layout = sheet_section_layout(fields) %>
<% repeats_page_title = section == local_assigns[:page_title] %>
<fieldset class="<%= local_assigns[:side_by_side] ? "min-w-0" : "mt-10 min-w-0 first-of-type:mt-0" %>">
  <legend class="<%= sheet_section_legend_classes(layout, repeats_page_title) %>"><%= section %></legend>
  <% if local_assigns[:lead] && %i[two_columns described_choices].exclude?(layout) && !sheet_lead_in_lists_column?(fields) %>
    <div class="clear-left max-w-sm"><%= lead %></div>
  <% end %>
  <%= render sheet_section_partial(layout),
             character: character, fields: fields, all_fields: all_fields, computed: computed,
             lead: local_assigns[:lead] %>
</fieldset>
